---

<Base title="Eben Thurston | SEO, SEM & AI Search Executive | Ex-TIAA" description={description}>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(schema)} slot="head" />

  <div class="hero">
    <div>
      <h1>Eben Thurston</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Eben Thurston is a search marketing executive with a pattern of
        arriving early to shifts in how people find things online. He wrote
        technical SEO standards before the discipline had a name, ran global
        search across 20+ languages and territories, and grew brand mentions in
        Google AI Overviews 1,714% at a Fortune 100 financial services firm.
      </p>
    </div>
    <img
      class="headshot"
      src="/eben-thurston.jpg"
      alt="Eben Thurston, search marketing executive based in New York"
      width="576"
      height="576"
      loading="eager"
    />
  </div>

  <h2 id="key-facts">Key Facts</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Started as a front-end developer, which still shapes how he works: close enough to the stack to write the technical requirements himself.</li>
    <li>Most recently Director, Integrated Search at TIAA (2024-2026), running organic and paid search across TIAA and Nuveen as a single commercial P&amp;L.</li>
    <li>Grew TIAA brand mentions in Google AI Overviews 1,714% to 10,865, and AI-referred sessions 1,214%.</li>
    <li>Grew organic clicks 528% year over year, with impressions up 655% on optimized pages.</li>
    <li>Expanded page-one keyword coverage 510% and outranked Fidelity, Vanguard, and Schwab on core terms.</li>
    <li>An early mover in Generative Engine Optimization, building an agency's inaugural generative AI practice within months of ChatGPT's launch.</li>
    <li>Led a 20-person cross-functional search team across New York and India serving a top-four US bank.</li>
    <li>Drove 30% YoY organic growth and 80% total demand growth at FULLBEAUTY Brands across 18 site migrations.</li>
    <li>Ran search as the top-producing channel at Shutterstock through its $170M to $425M revenue run.</li>
    <li>Two client properties he helped build were acquired: <a href="https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/webmd-acquires-additude-301299280.html">ADDitude Magazine (by WebMD)</a> and BobVila.com (by Recurrent Ventures).</li>
    <li>Began his career on Wall Street (Morgan Stanley, Lehman Brothers, Goldman Sachs). MBA, Fordham University.</li>
    <li>Played <a href="https://www.sports-reference.com/cbb/players/eben-thurston-1.html">Division I basketball</a> at the University of Vermont.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="cv">CV</h2>

  <h3>Fractional CMO &amp; Head of Growth, Purely Mat Pilates <span class="meta">(Nov 2025-present)</span></h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Leads customer acquisition and digital growth strategy, scaling a regional boutique studio into a web-based video subscription platform.</li>
    <li>Built and launched the platform architecture at <a href="https://purelymatpilates.com">purelymatpilates.com</a> with AI-assisted engineering tools, covering technical SEO, page speed, and schema architecture. Documented in <a href="/insights/geo-on-a-local-business-site/">GEO on a Local Business Site</a>.</li>
    <li>Manages local SEO, Google Business Profile optimization, and paid acquisition against studio retention and the subscription funnel.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Director, Integrated Search, TIAA <span class="meta">(2024-2026)</span></h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Ran a unified search engine across TIAA and Nuveen, managing organic and paid as one commercial P&amp;L at a Fortune 100 financial services firm.</li>
    <li>Grew brand mentions in Google AI Overviews 1,714% to 10,865 and AI-referred sessions 1,214% by building the technical and content frameworks for generative engine visibility.</li>
    <li>Lifted organic clicks 528% year over year, impressions 655% on optimized pages, page-one keyword coverage 510%, and the ranking keyword universe 106%.</li>
    <li>Outranked Fidelity, Vanguard, and Schwab on core category terms.</li>
    <li>Restructured paid search so Performance Max delivered 30% of account conversions on 25% of spend, at an 18% better CPA than account average and 28% better cost per account open than standard search.</li>
    <li>Ran the multi-channel demand engine for TIAA Wealth Management's "Invest in Your Worth" initiative across paid search, PMAX, LinkedIn, programmatic, and video, feeding IRA leads and advisor pipeline.</li>
    <li>Diagnosed and resolved a PMAX conversion-tagging failure that had suppressed attributed account opens by 53%, restoring data integrity and reported volume.</li>
    <li>Stood up week-over-week creative tracking that surfaced a 61% LinkedIn engagement gap, then moved budget toward variants outperforming benchmark by 8-91%.</li>
    <li>Held 99.9% budget delivery and closed December at 95% above the account-open goal.</li>
    <li>Ran early adopter tests of Google AI Max for Search.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Director, Search Marketing, iQuanti <span class="meta">(2021-2023)</span></h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Led a 20-person cross-functional team across New York and India serving a top-four US bank, aligning technical SEO, UX, legal, and content strategy.</li>
    <li>Beat 2022 traffic targets by 17% and SEO performance targets by 24%.</li>
    <li>Retained the full enterprise portfolio through the 2023 banking-sector volatility with zero churn.</li>
    <li>Founded the firm's inaugural generative AI practice following the release of ChatGPT and Bard, advising Fortune 500 financial clients on LLM visibility and brand protection.</li>
    <li>Authored the firm's research on Google SGE, establishing the ranking relationship between SGE citations and traditional top-three organic results.</li>
    <li>Built review workflows across SEO, Legal, and Compliance that raised speed to production in highly regulated banking environments.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Director, Digital Marketing / Director, SEO, FULLBEAUTY Brands <span class="meta">(2017-2020)</span></h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Co-led digital marketing across a 12+ brand portfolio, driving 30% year-over-year organic growth and 80% growth in total demand.</li>
    <li>Directed 18 site migrations, including eight to Salesforce Commerce Cloud, and owned the organic search P&amp;L.</li>
    <li>Led the ESP migration to Epsilon Harmony with segmentation, personalization, and automated product recommendations, delivering an average 2x increase in email revenue per brand.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Director, SEO &amp; Content Strategy, Fareportal <span class="meta">(2016-2017)</span></h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Architected a global SEO governance framework to rehabilitate domain authority in travel technology, recovering from legacy algorithmic penalties.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>SEO Product Owner, Global, Shutterstock <span class="meta">(2012-2016)</span></h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Search was the top-producing channel during the company's $170M to $425M revenue run.</li>
    <li>Ran a $30M paid media program alongside global organic search across 20+ languages and territories.</li>
    <li>A crawl and indexation fix drove a 300% lift in non-English traffic.</li>
    <li>Consolidating the Footage subdomain moved rankings from page two to top three and lifted SEO revenue 80%.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Founder &amp; Managing Director, Spring Marketing Strategies <span class="meta">(2009-2012)</span></h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Founded and scaled a digital consultancy serving 30+ retainer clients, including Time Inc. and Coola.</li>
    <li>Architected audience growth for BobVila.com (later acquired by Recurrent Ventures) and ADDitude Magazine (later <a href="https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/webmd-acquires-additude-301299280.html">acquired by WebMD</a>).</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Earlier roles</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Director, Marketing &amp; Audience Development at 1-800-FLOWERS.COM / Celebrations.com, where organic traffic grew 267% in four months.</li>
    <li>Managing Director, Digital Marketing at Root Markets, a mortgage lead exchange co-founded by <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lewis_Ranieri">Lewis Ranieri</a>, operating at the intersection of Wall Street securitization and digital customer acquisition.</li>
    <li>Time Inc., across web production, front-end development, web analytics, and business development, negotiating content and technology partnerships with Google, Facebook, and Yahoo.</li>
    <li>Wall Street foundations at Morgan Stanley, Lehman Brothers, and Goldman Sachs.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Education</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>MBA, <a href="https://www.fordham.edu/gabelli-school-of-business/">Fordham University, Graduate School of Business Administration (Gabelli School)</a> (Marketing; Product Management).</li>
    <li>BA, Political Science &amp; English, University of Vermont, where he played Division I basketball.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="faq">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
